# M1 / B002 — hooks (static analysis; not executed).

C R11 OL DEP-001,DEP-003,DEP-004,DEP-005 | MUST (PreToolUse deny until the add-dependency marker; PostToolUse feedback on changed dependency entries) | NuGet and npm dependency additions and updates go through the add-dependency workflow first (need and approval check, package choice, latest stable compatible version, deprecation, vulnerability and license checks); dependency commands are denied until the identical command is re-run with the trailing comment '# add-dependency: checked', and edited dependency entries trigger a reminder to confirm the workflow was applied. | Bash and PowerShell commands (dotnet, nuget, npm/pnpm/yarn, ng, PowerShell package cmdlets); manifest edits | The marker is self-certified; restore-only installs (npm ci, install without package names) are not gated.
C R13 OL GOV-009,GOV-007 | SHOULD (PostToolUse feedback; Stop reminder once per change state) | When SPECIFICATION.md changes, keep it consistent with CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md and the implementation and record approved behavior through the architecture-decision workflow. | edits of SPECIFICATION.md | Stop reminder repeats only for a changed state.
C R14 OL GOV-021 | SHOULD (PostToolUse feedback; Stop reminder once per change state) | When CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md changes, run the custom-settings workflow to synchronize every affected surface. | edits of CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md | Stop reminder repeats only for a changed state.
C R15 OL PST-008 | SHOULD (Stop reminder: Claude continues once per change state) | When persistence model files (Domain .cs, Infrastructure Persistence/Configurations) change without seed-data changes, confirm the persistence-change workflow (seed co-change) was applied, or state why it does not apply. | Stop in a Git work tree | Never re-blocks while stop_hook_active; repeats only when the content of the triggering files changes.
C R16 OL TST-009,TST-010 | SHOULD (Stop reminder once per change state) | When backend production code changed without backend test changes, check regression coverage and behavioral-probe preservation (development-workflow, verify) before finishing. | Stop in a Git work tree | Same repetition limits as R15.
C X8 EX ARC-020,ARC-001,GOV-017 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved; PreToolUse deny until the project-reference marker; PostToolUse routing of changed project files) | Changing the project reference graph is Reserved; project-reference commands are denied until the project-structure workflow was applied (re-run with '# project-reference: checked'), which routes Reserved reference-graph changes to architecture-decision; project files or references changed, removed or moved without a recognized command are reported for confirmation of the owning workflow. | .NET project references and project files | The marker is self-certified; references inside the frame's layout follow project-structure without a Decision Request. | ARC-020 requires approval for new layers/projects and ARC-001 constrains direction; no oracle policy makes individual reference edges between existing projects Reserved or gates every reference command. | A direction-legal reference outside the frame's layout needs a Decision Request, and every 'dotnet add reference' is denied until the marker is added.
C X9 EX - | MUST (PostToolUse feedback after instruction edits) | After an edit to an instruction file the instruction-structure check runs and its reported errors must be fixed (template-maintenance). | edits of instruction files | none stated | Instruction-system maintenance rule; no oracle policy regulates instruction-file structure. | Editing a rule so that an implementation name leaks outside its module produces blocking feedback that must be resolved.
C X10 EX PST-009,PST-010 | SHOULD (Stop reminder once per change state) | When persistence model files change without migration changes, confirm the persistence-change workflow (schema changes paired with migrations) was applied, or state why it does not apply. | Stop in a Git work tree | Same repetition limits as R15. | The oracle requires migrations only for schema-affecting CUSTOM_SETTINGS changes (PST-009) and review of generated migrations (PST-010); it has no general duty to pair model changes with migrations or to confirm schema impact at stop time. | Editing a Domain entity without a migration interrupts the stop once until the agent confirms whether the schema changed.

